<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      SPEC-06 (W5) — Policy-plane convergence.

      DECISION: Plane A (/api/agent-policies, hive_agent_policy) is canonical.
      Plane B (/api/ha-edr/policies, ha_agent_policy) is deprecated (config-only:
      no APPLY_POLICY push, no versioning, no device round-trip).

      Plane A's policy_config (schema v1) ALREADY models FIM file paths, registry
      keys, and collector toggles — see AgentPolicySchemaService — so NO new column
      is added to hive_agent_policy. Plane B's typed columns are projected into
      policy_config at the application layer by HaPolicyConvergenceMigrationRunner
      (idempotent, uses AgentPolicySchemaService.fromHaColumns). This changeset is
      the audit anchor for the convergence and a defensive guard; it makes no schema
      change and is a safe no-op where ha_agent_policy does not exist.

      Nothing is dropped here: the ha_agent_policy table and Plane B endpoints stay
      functional for a two-release deprecation window (LegacyHaEdrPolicyDeprecationFilter).
      A future changeset may drop ha_agent_policy once the deprecation window closes
      AND row-count is confirmed zero — never in this changeset.
    -->

    <!--
      Marker changeset. Runs once to record that the convergence has been applied
      in this environment; the actual row projection is app-level and idempotent so
      it also covers rows created after this migration but before the window closes.
      empty <comment> + no-op <sql> keeps liquibase:validate green with zero DDL.
    -->
    <changeSet id="20260914003-1" author="hivearmor">
        <comment>
            SPEC-06 W5: mark policy-plane convergence applied. Plane A
            (hive_agent_policy) canonical; Plane B (ha_agent_policy) deprecated.
            No schema change — Plane A policy_config already models FIM/registry/
            collectors. Row projection handled idempotently at the app layer.
        </comment>
        <!-- Intentionally no DDL/DML: schema is unchanged and Plane B rows are
             projected by the application runner (safe for the empty-table case). -->
        <sql>SELECT 1</sql>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
